<BehaviorPatch #track.r_2_0_2_6_-_0_6_-_2_1_-_1_7_3_0_-_a_d_d_-_m_o_d_e_l_i_n_g_-_v_a_l_i_d_a_t_e.behavior_patch.codument-core apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" { capability = "codument-core" } (
  <Mutations [
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://codument-core/requirements/modeling-validate" } (
      <Requirement #modeling-validate (
        <Statement ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJKZ>
        系统 SHALL provide an explicit `codument modeling validate` command that checks every modeling `.xnl` file across three layers — XNL syntax, node-schema semantics, and hierarchy/reference consistency — reporting issues author-friendly (file + line/position + reason) instead of throwing, gated behind `config/modeling.xml` (skipped when modeling is disabled).
        </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJKZ>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #syntax-layer { name = "Layer 1: XNL syntax" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #parse-and-report (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM0>
                A modeling `.xnl` file with an XNL syntax error (e.g. mismatched text marker, unclosed block).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM0>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM1>
                `codument modeling validate` runs.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM1>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM2>
                The system SHALL parse via xnl-core `parseXnl(.., {textBlockStyle:true})` and report `{file, line/position, reason}`, rather than letting an uncaught `XnlParseError` propagate.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM2>
                <Ands [
                  <And ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM3>
                  A syntactically valid file SHALL pass this layer with no finding.
                  </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM3>
                ]>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
          <Suite #schema-layer { name = "Layer 2: node-schema semantics" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #reuse-validate-node (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM4>
                A modeling node missing a minimal-required representation (e.g. `entity` without `types`/`fact_grade`/`single_writer`, or an unknown bare kind).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM4>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM5>
                validate runs.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM5>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM6>
                The system SHALL reuse `validateModelingNode` (kind spectrum, minimal representations, `fact_grade` enum, namespaced id) and surface each violation as a finding.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM6>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
          <Suite #hierarchy-layer { name = "Layer 3: hierarchy / definition consistency" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #id-path-alignment (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM7>
                A node whose id namespace does not match its file path `&lt;plane&gt;/&lt;context&gt;` (e.g. `#inventory.stock` inside `domain/orders/index.xnl`).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM7>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM8>
                validate runs.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM8>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM9>
                The system SHALL flag a hierarchy violation: the id's context segment MUST equal the path context, and if the id carries a plane prefix it MUST equal the path plane.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJM9>
              )>
              <Case #plane-legality (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMA>
                The modeling registry root and a file under some plane.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMA>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMB>
                validate runs.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMB>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMC>
                The system SHALL require a `domain` plane to exist and accept open derived planes, flagging an unknown plane per `config/modeling.xml` policy (default: warning).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMC>
              )>
              <Case #reference-resolvable (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMD>
                A node with a `modeling://` reference (`single_writer`/`depends_on`/`derived_from`/`uses`) pointing to a node absent from the registry index.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMD>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJME>
                validate runs over the full registry.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJME>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMF>
                The system SHALL resolve `modeling://` references (scheme self-identifying) against the registry index and report dangling references.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMF>
                <Ands [
                  <And ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMG>
                  `behavior://` references SHALL be syntax-checked but their existence MAY be left unverified (no hard dependency on the behaviors registry).
                  </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMG>
                ]>
              )>
              <Case #unique-id (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMH>
                Two nodes sharing the same id across files.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMH>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMJ>
                validate runs.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMJ>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMK>
                The system SHALL report the duplicate id with both file locations (as a finding, not an uncaught throw).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMK>
              )>
              <Case #delta-files-same-rules (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMM>
                A track's `modeling_deltas/&lt;plane&gt;/&lt;context&gt;.xnl` target-state file.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMM>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMN>
                validate runs against deltas (e.g. `modeling validate --deltas &lt;track&gt;`).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMN>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMP>
                The same syntax + schema + hierarchy rules SHALL apply, with the id namespace aligned to the delta file's `&lt;plane&gt;/&lt;context&gt;`.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMP>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
          <Suite #gating-and-report { name = "Gating and reporting" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #config-gate (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMQ>
                `config/modeling.xml` with modeling disabled (default).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMQ>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMR>
                `codument modeling validate` runs.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMR>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMS>
                The system SHALL skip and state modeling is disabled, consistent with `lint`/`track`/`archive` gating.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMS>
              )>
              <Case #issues-first-exit (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMT>
                One or more findings across layers.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMT>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMV>
                validate completes.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMV>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMW>
                The system SHALL print findings grouped by file with a non-zero summary count (issues-first), and a clean run SHALL report success.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMW>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://codument-core/requirements/xnl-format-guide" } (
      <Requirement #xnl-format-guide (
        <Statement ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMX>
        系统 SHALL vendor the xnl-core for-AI format guide into codument std as the authoritative XNL syntax reference for authoring modeling nodes, because the published npm package ships only `dist/` (its `doc/ai-guide/` is not packaged).
        </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMX>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #vendored-guide { name = "Vendored XNL format guide" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #guide-present (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMY>
                An AI author generating modeling XNL needs syntax rules (markers, zero-escape, EBNF, common errors).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMY>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMZ>
                It consults codument std.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJMZ>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN0>
                codument SHALL provide `std/spec/xnl-format.md` vendored from `xnl-core` `doc/ai-guide/XnlDataFormatForAi.md`, with a provenance note (source + version).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN0>
              )>
              <Case #modeling-specs-reference (
                <Given ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN1>
                The modeling specs (`modeling-registry.md` / `modeling-node-schema.md` / `modeling-delta.md`).
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN1>
                <When ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN2>
                They describe XNL writing.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN2>
                <Then ?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN3>
                They SHALL reference `std/spec/xnl-format.md` as the authoritative syntax source instead of re-deriving syntax inline.
                </?01M02NT0W8V81EVQKC9K65HJN3>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
  ]>
)>
